### Autoscaling

What does scaling mean?

Let’s go back to the time when applications were hosted on servers. What happens if the load on an application increases and there are no resources left? We would have to increase the server's physical resources—which first required shutting the server down. This is known as vertical scaling.

If an application can run as multiple instances, we can use horizontal scaling. This involves adding more servers and distributing the load among them.

In short, horizontal scaling consists of adding more resources to our application.
Horizontal autoscaling consists of automatically adding more instances or servers for our application.
